<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-3938] JDBC POJO store should support escaping for database schema, table and field names</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-3938</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Sometimes database names could be very &lt;b&gt;strange&lt;/b&gt; and this could be handled only via escaping. We need to support this.&lt;br/&gt;
Adding &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;String&lt;/span&gt; JdbcDialect.escape(name)&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt; method looks like a good solution.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="13006128">IGNITE-3938</key>
            <summary>JDBC POJO store should support escaping for database schema, table and field names</summary>
